From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ep9
Subject: [PATCH] icu_calendar: a binary search for the month count of
 `until`

ArithmeticDate::until finds the month count with the spec loop of
NonISODateUntil: from a lower bound (C::min_months_from), one
NonISODateSurpasses check per month until one surpasses. Each check
balances the months one year at a time (new_balanced), so it is
O(years). For the East Asian calendars min_months_from is
12 * years + years / 3, about 0.035 months per year below the true
rate (about 12.368), so the loop runs O(years) passes: O(years^2) in
all (chinese, largestUnit "months": 20,000 years 1.7-4.9 s; the full
Temporal range more than 120 s), with no way for an embedder to stop
it.

NonISODateSurpasses is monotone in the month count, so the last count
that does not surpass is the same for a binary search between the
lower bound (it does not surpass) and 13 months per year of the year
difference plus one year (it surpasses). The result is the same; the
search takes O(log(months)) checks, so O(years log years) in all. If
the bound does not surpass (not reached for valid dates) the spec loop
runs from there.

Test: in ep9, crates/ep9_temporal/tests/calendars.rs (equal results
with the loop on 446 pairs per calendar; chinese and dangi over
20,000 years).
---
 .../calendar/src/calendar_arithmetic.rs       | 36 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/calendar/src/calendar_arithmetic.rs b/components/calendar/src/calendar_arithmetic.rs
index a2cb514..08ef7d9 100644
--- a/components/calendar/src/calendar_arithmetic.rs
+++ b/components/calendar/src/calendar_arithmetic.rs
@@ -1039,9 +1039,41 @@ impl<C: DateFieldsResolver> ArithmeticDate<C> {
                 candidate_months = min_months
             }
 
-            while !surpasses_checker.surpasses_months(candidate_months) {
+            // Non-spec optimization: NonISODateSurpasses is monotone in the month count (the
+            // first month of y0 + m0 + months only moves away from `self` as months grows in
+            // the direction of sign), so the spec loop stops at the last candidate that does
+            // not surpass, and a binary search finds the same value. The loop took one pass
+            // per month past `candidate_months`, and each pass balances the months one year at
+            // a time; with a lower bound whose error grows with the year count (the East Asian
+            // `min_months_from`) that was O(years^2). The search takes O(log(months)) passes.
+            if !surpasses_checker.surpasses_months(candidate_months) {
                 months = candidate_months;
-                candidate_months += sign;
+                // No date pair is more than 13 months per year apart, plus one year for the
+                // partial years at the ends: this candidate surpasses.
+                let span = (other.year() - self.year()).unsigned_abs();
+                let bound = i32::try_from(13 * (u64::from(span) + 1) + 1).unwrap_or(i32::MAX);
+                let mut surpassing = sign * bound;
+                if (surpassing - months) * sign <= 0
+                    || !surpasses_checker.surpasses_months(surpassing)
+                {
+                    // Not reached for valid dates; the spec loop from here keeps the result.
+                    debug_assert!(false, "the month bound does not surpass");
+                    candidate_months = months + sign;
+                    while !surpasses_checker.surpasses_months(candidate_months) {
+                        months = candidate_months;
+                        candidate_months += sign;
+                    }
+                    surpassing = candidate_months;
+                }
+                // Invariant: `months` does not surpass, `surpassing` does.
+                while (surpassing - months) * sign > 1 {
+                    let mid = months + (surpassing - months) / 2;
+                    if surpasses_checker.surpasses_months(mid) {
+                        surpassing = mid;
+                    } else {
+                        months = mid;
+                    }
+                }
             }
         }
         // Freeze the checker's Months field state.
